hello and welcome to Playstation grenade  three months ago I made contact with  scuff the manufacturers behind the  controller's used by so many pro ps4 and  Xbox one players my task was simple I  wanted to know if their controllers  could make me a better player at  fortnight I watched countless reviews of  scuff controllers online and either  found the reviewer slating the product  without explaining the issues are worse  still the reviewer was partnered with  scuff leading me to distrust them even  though they were endorsing a product  they believed in wholeheartedly scoff  kindly sent an impact controller in  bright pink because I have an unhealthy  obsession with that color but more  importantly they have given me free rein  in my review and not attempted to  contact me during the review process so  please let me stage once and for all I  am NOT sponsored bicycie all opinions  are my own so after three months of use  the plan is to go through the great  things that scuff impact controllers  offer but also a few issues i've  encounters so with that out of the way  let's do this the first thing we need to  do is understand why scuff controllers  are used by professional gamers it comes  down to one important feature the  ability to keep both thumbs on the  sticks at all times some simple I know  but this small fact is what gives a  gamer a huge advantage on the  battlefield let's break it down on the  back of the scuf controller are these  paddles which act in the same way as  face buttons so on the ps4 that's the X  square circle and triangle buttons which  can be accessed from underneath the  controller depending on the size of your  hands your natural grip will see your  middle finger or ring finger rest  perfectly on the plastic buttons let's  take a typical shotgun fight in Battle  Royale  most of the time we all jump around like  headless chickens jumping helps in two  ways it makes us a harder target and if  we manage to get the higher ground  it makes head shots easier here's the  issue to jump with a standard controller  you'd need to take your thumb off the  right stick to press jump not only does  it slow us down eat also makes aiming  the shotgun impossible whilst jumping  unless you use the claw technique but  that is extremely uncomfortable for the  majority of gamers so by having a button  underneath the pad we can jump and aim  simultaneously giving us a huge  advantage in gunfights some would say  it's unfair and I kind of agree it's a  little ok to say the least  depending on the model of scuff we look  at there'll be two or four puddles to  use for context the infinity natively  has X and circle mapped on the rear  whereas the impact has triangle of  square to here's where things in  fortnight can be made ridiculously easy  with a scuf controller on a standard  controller building a one by one can  take a great deal of toll on your right  thumb as switching to build mode and  jumping and aiming with precision is  difficult to master  whereas on the impact all three of those  buttons are immediately accessed by  different fingers jump is controlled by  your middle finger on the left hand  build mode is controlled by the middle  finger on the right hand and aiming  remained safely under your right thumb  this change may only save a tenth of a  second each time but this time adds up  especially in build battles and the  freedom to instantly switch weapon to  jump and aim is frankly awesome when  buying a scuf it's also possible to  purchase a remapping tool just in case  you want to customize your experience  sadly that does cost a little more but  we'll get to that very soon oh another  quick note it isn't possible to map  combinations on macros to the paddles I  had hoped to map the perfect three tile  high one by one tower for clutch build  offs alas it's not possible at present  but imagine that complex movements in a  single button press yeah if we break you  down like that that probably is too far  that would be a little too close to  cheating surprisingly the greatest thing  I found on the scuff impact was not the  under pedals but instead the  hair-trigger option depending on the  game r2 or the right bumper it's almost  always the gun trigger it was even  reshaped to feel more akin to a real gun  trigger the time it takes to push down  completely can cause a missed shot or  two  the impact offers a hair-trigger option  to minimize the button depth with this  small adjustment is possible to create a  shallower button press making shots that  millisecond quicker in battle this  function improved my sniping hugely in  fortnight and I found switching back to  a standard controller I really missed  this option another great addition to  the scuff controllers are the options of  thumb sticks because scuff offer custom  modular elements to each controller from  color to length of the bumper buttons  it's easy to overlook the thumb sticks  without a doubt the thumb sticks make a  difference they can be domed like the  ps3 pads they can be concave like ps4  pads they can be made longer they can be  colored differently but it's  surprisingly it's the material which I  was most impressed with and  scientist so I can't really break it  down but the thumbsticks use a type of  rubber which clings to your thumb when  in a build battle with sweaty palms and  sweaty fingers and thumbs the rubberized  thumb sticks prevent any slipping from  my grip  there's even an option on the impact to  give the controller additional grip I  personally didn't get that option but I  can definitely see the appeal  so we've outlined the great elements  that make a scuf controller the  preferred option by most pro console  players but all that customization and  modulation is also an area to be  concerned with the scuff impact starts  off costing more than twice the amount  of a standard controller the cost  balloons further with every option you  add on I priced up the controller scuff  sent to me and it would have cost 200  pounds after-tax instead of translating  that into your currency I'll convert the  currency instead this one bloody good  pad is the same price as for standard  controllers to put that bluntly the only  way to look at this is to see a scuf  controller as an investment we can  change the way we look at scuff  controllers again by isolating each part  for example when the paddles wear away  it's possible to purchase more on the  star it's modular remember so we can  take off any part we like and replace it  with newer pieces I noticed in most  reviews that our against scuff  controllers they are usually due to a  device not working as intended I can  completely understand where this opinion  comes from as when my controller arrived  the right thumbstick kept sticking my  first reaction would have been more  furious if I had spent the money myself  but as this was a review model I saw  this as an opportunity I have to admit  it was not pleasant using tech support  but once I found a real human being  things moved much more quickly sending  the controller back though would have  seen it gone for several weeks as that  wasn't an option for me I decided to  take off the thumb sticks to  troubleshoot the problem and when I  reassembled the controller by switching  the sticks around somehow the issue was  gone it just wasn't there anymore  and it worked perfectly to some that  will sound absolutely whirring whereas  others will just see that as a good  thing I'm not sure how I feel about it  but wanting to make sure you had all the  information just in case you are  thinking about making this choice  another issue I discovered was a slight  delay or unresponsive button presses on  the back paddles once again this could  have broken me could have sent me into a  mad rage and I could have been one of  those people you see on youtubes  completely slating the product but that  said it was unbelievably easy to fix the  back paddles were dirty and needed to be  cleaned so I got out a cotton bud or a  q-tip and in a couple of swipes it was  clean again that took me ten hours to  figure out by the way before we recap  everything let's look at form factor the  current models on the market are the  impact and the Infinity in retrospect I  should have chosen the Infinity as my  hands fit better around the original ps4  controller after using a friend's  Infiniti I quickly realized that was the  better option for me in terms of comfort  saying that the additional paddles on  the impact are excellent and if you were  or are an Xbox player this updated form  factor will feel most comfortable to you  either way keep in mind how many hours  you'll need to put in to acquire the  muscle memory to use these to the  fullest anything from 60 to 600 hours so  it's an investment in money and it's an  investment in time in conclusion the  awesome hair-trigger system the  brilliant under pedals the slightly  sticky thumb sticks for grips the custom  colors the modular system are all  fantastic reasons to buy a scuff impact  controller but on the other hand the  slightly cheap plastic feel the  potential issue of one of the parts  arriving untested and of course the high  price tag our issues I think you should  be aware of and although this was a  review of the scuff impact we started  with an original question can a scuf  controller make you better at fortnight  quick building yes quick shooting yes  improved aim and jumping yes without a  doubt yes a scuf controller can make you  better at the fortnight hopefully that  will show you both sides of the argument  and put you in better stead to make a  decision on a pro controller there are  other pro controllers on the market and  if I get my hands on any of those I will  compare and contrast as many as I can  but as scuf were the only company kind  enough to send me one of their review  models I wanted to also show you the  future of their products this is the  scuff Vantage offering improved  precision and control much more  comfortable to hold I'm told offset  thumb sticks like an Xbox controller and  all the customization scuff is renowned  for I'll do my best to get my hands on  this beast and if I do I'll be back with  an objective review later in the year I  imagine from PlayStation granade it's  been an absolute pleasure I'll see you  next time  [Music]
 

